# CR 702.88c: instances of rebound on one spell are redundant - one exile, one delayed trigger. Bot1 casts Ojer Pakpatiq on turn 1,
# then Ephemerate (rebound printed) on it on turn 3 with Mox Pearl: the trigger gives it a second instance. It is exiled once and,
# at the next upkeep (turn 5), Bot1 is offered one cast from exile for nothing. That cast was not from a hand, so Ephemerate goes
# to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ojer Pakpatiq, Deepest Epoch
Ephemerate
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

